Definition

Mogri is the irreducible coined root for a held-open condition in which an important semantic object, intent, possibility, or partly inaccessible phenomenon remains available before a useful distinction is fixed.

The object may be unresolved, unspecified, disputed, incomplete, or still changing. Mogri lets it remain available without forcing a category, answer, role, cause, or final interpretation.

In technical use, Mogri can serve as a foundational conceptual or cognitive container: a named zero-stage or runtime condition in which the unresolved object can be held without being replaced by a nearby answer.

Mogri is not derivative from other CSP primitives.

The name was recovered through the word-history route:

`transmogrification -> mogrification -> mogri`

That is etymological provenance. It does not make Mogri semantically compositional from other primitives.

Origin phrase

An early coinage line was:

`mogrification = the inexplicability of existence itself, in motion`

That line records the discovery intuition: actuality can outrun explanation.

It is not a claim that reality literally requires a Mogri container.

Boundary

Mogri is not:

- an entity
- an actor
- a force
- a cause
- a generator of later states
- a hidden memory store
- a bag containing every unknown fact
- a synonym for confusion
- a synonym for mystery
- permanent refusal to decide

Mogri does not make the later distinction happen.
Mogri does not decide what the object will become.
Mogri does not require the object to remain unresolved forever.

Resolution is allowed when evidence, user intent, or another valid local condition supports it.

Object note

In these specifications, `object` means the semantic or task object being handled. It does not claim that physical things contain Mogri.

Simple English

Mogri is the part that lets an important thing stay unresolved without making up the answer.

Operational test

A system is behaving in a Mogri-compatible way when:

- the active unresolved object remains available
- later material does not silently replace it
- uncertainty is not converted into invented certainty
- a real distinction can still be made when support arrives

A system is not demonstrating Mogri merely because it can list unknowns or unfinished tasks.

Compact form

`MOGRI = irreducible held-open container for important unresolved potential; not derivative; not entity; not cause; no forced distinction`
